{"enableSqlExpressions() returns false unconditionally and inverts the sqlExpressions flag into a misleading local variable, making the toggle ineffective and guaranteeing QueryTypeSQL is always rejected even if sqlExpressions is enabled globally": 0.8930484056472778, "Stub DB implementation with methods returning 'not implemented' is still invoked by TablesList() and SQLCommand.Execute(), causing runtime failures if SQL expressions are accidentally re-enabled rather than being blocked at feature boundary": 0.817038357257843, "SQL expressions are rejected with different errors depending on which parsing path is active: new parser returns 'sqlExpressions is not implemented' while legacy path returns generic 'error reading SQL command', making user-facing behavior unpredictable": 0.602841854095459, "The enableSqlExpressions check was added only to ReadQuery path in reader.go, but legacy buildCMDNode path in nodes.go calls UnmarshalSQLCommand directly without equivalent gate, creating inconsistent security gate placement": 0.6581932902336121}